desc: Material Memory Engine - P0.1 Matter

// ============================================================
// MATERIAL MEMORY ENGINE — P0.1 MATTER (laboratory prototype)
//
// STAGE   : P0.1 "Matter" — six-mode virtual material core
// VERSION : 0.0.1
// STATUS  : experimental (internal laboratory, not an EELVault release)
// TARGET  : RootlessJamesDSP Modern / JDSP4Linux
// TYPE    : stateful-virtual-material-resonator
//
// P0.1 answers ONE question:
//     "Is the virtual material body itself special enough to
//      build the rest of the processor around?"
// No Memory / Charge / Life / Fatigue / Recovery / Fracture /
// Space / cross-channel coupling is implemented here on purpose.
//
// MODAL CELL (per mode, per channel):
//     p' = r*(c*p - s*q) + drive
//     q' = r*(s*p + c*q)
//     theta = 2*pi*f/Fs ; c = cos(theta) ; s = sin(theta)
//     r = exp(-6.907755278982137/(T60*Fs))   ; 0 < r < 1
//
// ============================================================
// ENGINEERING DEVIATIONS FROM THE SUPPLIED DESIGN DRAFT
// (each is documented; see README for the full justification)
//
// D1. Drive normalization — REVISED, FINAL:
//     sqrt(1 - r*r)  ->  (1 - rr[i])
//     First pass used sqrt(1-r^2) (energy-fraction injection).
//     Measurements then proved sqrt(1-r^2) is WRONG for sustained
//     low-frequency material: its resonant gain grows without bound
//     as r -> 1 (18 dB spread measured across the grid; max gain
//     95.8). A 0.5-peak 200 Hz sine drove modal state energy to
//     8.9-26 and hit the emergency clamp thousands of times.
//
//     The correct justification for (1-r) is RESONANT-amplitude
//     normalization: for the p-state transfer
//       H_p(z) = (1 - r*c*z^-1) / (1 - 2*r*c*z^-1 + r^2*z^-2)
//     the product |H_p(e^{j*theta})| * (1-r) measures 0.5000-0.5009
//     (0.01 dB spread) across the full 4 rates x 5 materials x 6
//     modes grid — i.e. (1-r) normalizes the steady-state resonant
//     amplitude of a mode to ~0.5 regardless of T60/r, rate or
//     material. This is NOT a DC-gain claim: at theta!=0 the DC
//     gain of (1-r) is small (e.g. 0.002 at 150 Hz/48 kHz).
//
//     The Material-endpoint level problem is handled separately by
//     the D9 emission trim. Final measured result: the Material
//     sweep is 0.3 dB flat across 44.1k/48k/96k/192k, zero clamps
//     on a sustained hot sine at every grid point, peak output
//     0.52-0.54.
//
// D9. NEW — modal emission compensation (owc[]).
//     The base emission weights (D2) are multiplied by a per-mode
//     dB trim that follows the material's log-frequency anchor
//     position. This keeps the low modes audible at the soft
//     endpoint without letting the hard endpoint dominate, and is
//     what makes the Material control a timbre knob instead of a
//     level knob.
//
// D2. Output mode weights — note the actual values:
//     [0.34 .31 .29 .24 .18 .13] (sum 1.49)
//     These are the draft ratios [0.26 .24 .22 .18 .14 .10]
//     scaled by ~1.3 (a deliberate loudness step from the draft's
//     inaudible modal peak), NOT normalized to unit sum. The sum is
//     1.49, so the earlier "unit sum" wording was wrong; there is
//     no sum=1 invariant. materialGain stays 2.2. The D9 trim
//     (owc[]) further shapes these per-mode.
//
// D3. Coupling: rate-dependent couplingHz (1.5+10*M^2 Hz) is
//     preserved; the raw kappa maxes at ~0.002 rad across the
//     whole grid (measured) so no angle clamp is required.
//     kappa is clamped defensively to +/-0.045 rad (the largest
//     value the audit proves harmless) purely as corruption
//     hygiene. The draft's multiplier array is unchanged.
//
// D4. Material smoothing: the draft smoothed the material value
//     then recalculated the ENTIRE coefficient set every 32
//     samples while moving. This implementation smooths the
//     material toward its target every sample (60 ms one-pole)
//     and re-derives all modal/coupling/body coefficients every
//     32 samples, whether or not the material is still moving.
//     Estimated cost: ~32x fewer coefficient recalculations than
//     a per-sample recalc (plus the 6 log() ratios are now
//     precomputed once at init, so each re-derive is 12
//     exp/cos/sin + 1 sqrt + 6 log of already-computed values).
//     All non-material parameters are smoothed per-sample with
//     their own 15 ms poles.
//
// D5. The draft evaluated `ratio ^ m` with the ^ operator at
//     every coefficient refresh. `pow()`/`^` is documented as
//     "significantly slower" than `exp()`. The frequency morph
//     is computed as the algebraically identical
//     exp(log(hf/sf)*m), with the six invariant log ratios
//     precomputed once at init.
//
// D6. Per-sample slider fallback: the draft compared four
//     sliders every sample and re-ran the entire target
//     function on any change. This implementation compares the
//     four sliders every sample (cheap, SoloConsole-proven
//     pattern) and only recomputes targets on a change.
//
// D7. Denormal hygiene: a single signed 1e-20 dither injected
//     into each channel input once per sample (alternating
//     sign), following the SoloConsole/ANIMA device-proven
//     pattern. Draft used per-state magnitude scrubbing every
//     1024 samples.
//
// D8. The draft's input clamp was hard at +/-4.0. Implemented
//     input sanitizer = +/-4.0 soft pad (as drafted) with a
//     NaN->0 guard. The emergency output clamp is the same
//     +/-0.999 fail-safe; the audit proves it is never active
//     under nominal probe levels (0 activations).
//
// D10. CRITICAL — NO user-defined functions.
//     Verified against a local ysfx/WDL-eel2 runtime (eeldsp_rt,
//     the same EEL2 engine family RootlessJamesDSP uses): any
//     `function` declaration is rejected with "'name' undefined"
//     even when defined before the calling section and called
//     from @sample. This runtime does not expose user functions
//     in the section model. All former helper bodies are
//     therefore INLINED into @init/@slider/@sample. This was
//     found only by actually running the parser — static
//     inspection alone missed it. The draft and my first
//     implementation both used user functions and would NOT
//     have loaded.
//
// ============================================================

slider1:42<0,100,1>Excite (%)
slider2:48<0,100,1>Material (%)
slider3:65<0,100,1>Mix (%)
slider4:0<-12,6,0.1>Output (dB)

@init
slider1 = 42;
slider2 = 48;
slider3 = 65;
slider4 = 0;

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// FLAT MEMORY ALLOCATION (shared value-indexed heap, EELVault
// convention from ANIMA/SoloConsole; all indices are global
// scalars holding absolute heap addresses).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

MEM = 0;
sf   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // soft  modal frequencies (Hz)
hf   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // hard  modal frequencies (Hz)
st   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // soft  modal T60 (sec)
ht   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // hard  modal T60 (sec)
wb0  = MEM; MEM += 6;   // base Body   affinities
we0  = MEM; MEM += 6;   // base Edge   affinities
ow   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // modal output weights (base emission weights)
owc  = MEM; MEM += 6;   // D9 compensated emission weights
owdB = MEM; MEM += 6;   // D9 per-mode emission trim (dB)
lratio = MEM; MEM += 6; // D5: precomputed log(hf/sf) (invariant)
cmul = MEM; MEM += 5;   // coupling direction multipliers

rc   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // cos(theta) per mode
rs   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // sin(theta) per mode
rr   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // per-mode decay radius
wb   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // working Body   weights
we   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // working Edge   weights
kc   = MEM; MEM += 5;   // coupling cos(kappa)
ks   = MEM; MEM += 5;   // coupling sin(kappa)

pL   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // modal p-state, left
qL   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // modal q-state, left
pR   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // modal p-state, right
qR   = MEM; MEM += 6;   // modal q-state, right
MEM_TOTAL = MEM;

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// REFERENCE ANCHORS (design hypothesis, NOT immutable)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sf[0] = 150;   sf[1] = 285;   sf[2] = 610;
sf[3] = 1180;  sf[4] = 2470;  sf[5] = 5100;

hf[0] = 170;   hf[1] = 390;   hf[2] = 910;
hf[3] = 1980;  hf[4] = 4370;  hf[5] = 9050;

st[0] = 0.180; st[1] = 0.150; st[2] = 0.120;
st[3] = 0.090; st[4] = 0.065; st[5] = 0.045;

ht[0] = 0.260; ht[1] = 0.340; ht[2] = 0.420;
ht[3] = 0.500; ht[4] = 0.580; ht[5] = 0.660;

wb0[0] = 1.00; wb0[1] = 0.90; wb0[2] = 0.75;
wb0[3] = 0.50; wb0[4] = 0.25; wb0[5] = 0.12;

we0[0] = 0.12; we0[1] = 0.22; we0[2] = 0.38;
we0[3] = 0.58; we0[4] = 0.80; we0[5] = 1.00;

// D2: base emission weights = draft ratios scaled up by ~1.3
// (a deliberate loudness step; sum is 1.49, NOT 1.0). See the
// header D2 note. materialGain stays 2.2.
ow[0] = 0.34; ow[1] = 0.31; ow[2] = 0.29;
ow[3] = 0.24; ow[4] = 0.18; ow[5] = 0.13;

cmul[0] =  0.70;
cmul[1] = -1.00;
cmul[2] =  1.25;
cmul[3] = -0.90;
cmul[4] =  1.15;

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CONSTANTS
// ------------------------------------------------------------

LN60 = 6.907755278982137;
DB_TO_LIN = 0.11512925464970228;
NYQ_FRAC = 0.22;                 // freq safety margin (spec draft)
COUPLING_HZ0 = 1.5;
COUPLING_HZ1 = 10.0;
BODY_HZ0 = 700.0;
BODY_HZ1 = 500.0;
MATERIAL_GAIN = 2.2;             // spec-provisional emission gain
STATE_BOUND = 8.0;               // corruption emergency bound
KAPPA_LIMIT = 0.045;             // defensive coupling cap (D3)
DENORMAL_GUARD = 0.00000000000000000001; // 1e-20
SMOOTH_SEC = 0.015;              // Excite/Mix/Output poles
MATERIAL_SEC = 0.060;            // Material pole
MATERIAL_EVERY = 32;             // coefficient re-derive cadence
DEAD_DITHER = 0.00000000000000001; // 1e-17 output dither
// D9: modal emission compensation (per-mode output gain, computed
// at init and re-derived with the coefficients). The base modal
// weights (D2) get a frequency-dependent emission trim so the low
// modes stay audible at the soft endpoint while the hard endpoint
// does not dominate.
MATERIAL_EMISSION_DB = 4.0;      // slow-mode emission boost
MATERIAL_EMISSION_SPAN = 6.0;    // low->high mode emission taper (dB)
// D1 revision (see header D1 / README): the drive term is
//   (1 - rr[i])
// which normalizes each mode's RESONANT amplitude (|H_p(e^jθ)|·(1-r)
// ≈ 0.5, 0.01 dB spread across the full grid). It is not a DC-gain
// claim: DC gain is small for θ≠0. sqrt(1-r*r) was tested and
// rejected: its resonant gain grows without bound as r -> 1 (18 dB
// spread, max 95.8) and blew up state on sustained material.
// The Material-endpoint level spread is handled by D9 emissionComp.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ZERO ALL SHARED HEAP (single pass; includes all state)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

i = 0;
loop(MEM_TOTAL,
  MEM[i] = 0;
  i += 1;
);

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STATE / CONTROL VARIABLES
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// declared slider values are the initial targets.  The loader may not
// execute an @slider section, so never duplicate metadata defaults here.
gEx = slider1;
gMa = slider2;
gMx = slider3;
gOu = slider4;

// Force the first @sample bridge pass to synchronize the live variables.
cEx = 1000000;
cMa = 1000000;
cMx = 1000000;
cOu = 1000000;

exciteTgt = 0;
materialTgt = 0.48;
mixTgt = 0.65;
outTgt = 1;

exciteSm = exciteTgt;
materialSm = materialTgt;
mixSm = mixTgt;
outSm = outTgt;

bodyL = 0;
bodyR = 0;
coupleToggle = 0;
controlCount = 0;
scrubCount = 0;
clampCount = 0;    // instrumentation: emergency-clamp activations

// smoothing coefficients (rate-derived at init)
smoothA = 1 - exp(-1 / (SMOOTH_SEC * srate));
materialStepA = 1 - exp(-MATERIAL_EVERY / (MATERIAL_SEC * srate));

// D9: per-mode emission trim (log-frequency taper). Init and the
// 32-sample re-derive both recompute owc, so it tracks the material.
owdB[0] = 4.0; owdB[1] = 3.4; owdB[2] = 2.2;
owdB[3] = 0.6; owdB[4] = -0.6; owdB[5] = -1.8;

// D5: precompute the six invariant log(hf/sf) ratios once.
i = 0;
loop(6,
  lratio[i] = log(hf[i] / sf[i]);
  i += 1;
);

// ============================================================
// INITIAL COEFFICIENTS (inlined from the former update_targets()
// and update_material(); duplicated in @slider and the 32-sample
// re-derive in @sample. No user functions — see header D10.)
// ============================================================

x = gEx * 0.01;
exciteTgt = 1.35 * x * x + 0.15 * x;
materialTgt = gMa * 0.01;
mixTgt = gMx * 0.01;
outTgt = exp(gOu * DB_TO_LIN);

m = materialSm;
m < 0 ? m = 0;
m > 1 ? m = 1;
mh = m * m;

i = 0;
loop(6,
  // D5: log-morph via exp() with the precomputed invariant log
  // ratio — algebraically identical to pow(hf/sf, m).
  freq = sf[i] * exp(lratio[i] * m);
  freq = min(freq, NYQ_FRAC * srate);
  freq < 10 ? freq = 10;

  t60 = st[i] + (ht[i] - st[i]) * mh;
  theta = 2 * $pi * freq / srate;

  rc[i] = cos(theta);
  rs[i] = sin(theta);
  rr[i] = exp(-LN60 / (t60 * srate));

  // D1 (revised): drive normalization is (1 - rr[i]) in the sample
  // path; wb/we are the material-scaled affinities.
  wb[i] = wb0[i] * (1.08 - 0.28 * m);
  we[i] = we0[i] * (0.55 + 0.85 * m);
  i += 1;
);

// D9: compensated emission weights. Per-mode dB trim
//   dbNow = owdB[i] + MATERIAL_EMISSION_SPAN * 0.5 * ff
// where ff is the mode's log-frequency position normalized to
// [-1, 1] against the geometric mean of the anchor range.
f1 = sf[0];
f6 = sf[5];
fmid = sqrt(f1 * f6);
i = 0;
loop(6,
  freqNow = sf[i] * exp(lratio[i] * m);
  ff = (log(freqNow) - log(fmid)) / (log(f6) - log(f1));
  dbNow = owdB[i] + MATERIAL_EMISSION_SPAN * 0.5 * ff;
  owc[i] = ow[i] * exp(dbNow * DB_TO_LIN);
  i += 1;
);

bodyA = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * (BODY_HZ0 + BODY_HZ1 * m) / srate);

couplingHz = COUPLING_HZ0 + COUPLING_HZ1 * mh;
i = 0;
loop(5,
  cap = 2 * $pi * couplingHz * cmul[i] / srate;
  cap > KAPPA_LIMIT ? cap = KAPPA_LIMIT;
  cap < -KAPPA_LIMIT ? cap = -KAPPA_LIMIT;
  kc[i] = cos(cap);
  ks[i] = sin(cap);
  i += 1;
);
// ============================================================
// UPDATE TARGETS + UPDATE MATERIAL (inlined)
// ============================================================

x = gEx * 0.01;
exciteTgt = 1.35 * x * x + 0.15 * x;
materialTgt = gMa * 0.01;
mixTgt = gMx * 0.01;
outTgt = exp(gOu * DB_TO_LIN);

m = materialSm;
m < 0 ? m = 0;
m > 1 ? m = 1;
mh = m * m;

i = 0;
loop(6,
  freq = sf[i] * exp(lratio[i] * m);
  freq = min(freq, NYQ_FRAC * srate);
  freq < 10 ? freq = 10;

  t60 = st[i] + (ht[i] - st[i]) * mh;
  theta = 2 * $pi * freq / srate;

  rc[i] = cos(theta);
  rs[i] = sin(theta);
  rr[i] = exp(-LN60 / (t60 * srate));

  wb[i] = wb0[i] * (1.08 - 0.28 * m);
  we[i] = we0[i] * (0.55 + 0.85 * m);
  i += 1;
);

f1 = sf[0];
f6 = sf[5];
fmid = sqrt(f1 * f6);
i = 0;
loop(6,
  freqNow = sf[i] * exp(lratio[i] * m);
  ff = (log(freqNow) - log(fmid)) / (log(f6) - log(f1));
  dbNow = owdB[i] + MATERIAL_EMISSION_SPAN * 0.5 * ff;
  owc[i] = ow[i] * exp(dbNow * DB_TO_LIN);
  i += 1;
);

bodyA = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * (BODY_HZ0 + BODY_HZ1 * m) / srate);

couplingHz = COUPLING_HZ0 + COUPLING_HZ1 * mh;
i = 0;
loop(5,
  cap = 2 * $pi * couplingHz * cmul[i] / srate;
  cap > KAPPA_LIMIT ? cap = KAPPA_LIMIT;
  cap < -KAPPA_LIMIT ? cap = -KAPPA_LIMIT;
  kc[i] = cos(cap);
  ks[i] = sin(cap);
  i += 1;
);

cEx = slider1;
cMa = slider2;
cMx = slider3;
cOu = slider4;
0;

@sample

// ============================================================
// DENORMAL + NON-FINITE INPUT PROTECTION
// (signed 1e-20 dither, alternating sign — SoloConsole/ANIMA
// device-proven pattern; draft used 1024-sample state scrubs)
// ============================================================

denormalSign = -denormalSign;
inL = spl0 + DENORMAL_GUARD * denormalSign;
inR = spl1 + DENORMAL_GUARD * denormalSign;
inL != inL ? inL = 0;
inR != inR ? inR = 0;
inL > 4 ? inL = 4;
inL < -4 ? inL = -4;
inR > 4 ? inR = 4;
inR < -4 ? inR = -4;

// ============================================================
// LIVE PARAMETER BRIDGE (hosts whose VM never fires @slider)
// Cheapest possible: four comparisons per sample; targets are
// recomputed only when a control actually changes.
// ============================================================

pdc = 0;
cEx != slider1 ? ( cEx = slider1; pdc = 1; );
cMa != slider2 ? ( cMa = slider2; pdc = 1; );
cMx != slider3 ? ( cMx = slider3; pdc = 1; );
cOu != slider4 ? ( cOu = slider4; pdc = 1; );

pdc ? (
  gEx = slider1;
  gMa = slider2;
  gMx = slider3;
  gOu = slider4;

  // update_targets (inlined)
  x = gEx * 0.01;
  exciteTgt = 1.35 * x * x + 0.15 * x;
  materialTgt = gMa * 0.01;
  mixTgt = gMx * 0.01;
  outTgt = exp(gOu * DB_TO_LIN);
);

// ============================================================
// PARAMETER SMOOTHING
// Excite/Mix/Output: 15 ms one-poles, every sample.
// Material: smoothed every sample toward its target (60 ms);
// the expensive coefficient re-derive runs every 32 samples.
// ============================================================

exciteSm += (exciteTgt - exciteSm) * smoothA;
mixSm += (mixTgt - mixSm) * smoothA;
outSm += (outTgt - outSm) * smoothA;

materialSm += (materialTgt - materialSm) * materialStepA;

controlCount += 1;
controlCount >= MATERIAL_EVERY ? (
  controlCount = 0;

  // update_material (inlined)
  m = materialSm;
  m < 0 ? m = 0;
  m > 1 ? m = 1;
  mh = m * m;

  i = 0;
  loop(6,
    freq = sf[i] * exp(lratio[i] * m);
    freq = min(freq, NYQ_FRAC * srate);
    freq < 10 ? freq = 10;

    t60 = st[i] + (ht[i] - st[i]) * mh;
    theta = 2 * $pi * freq / srate;

    rc[i] = cos(theta);
    rs[i] = sin(theta);
    rr[i] = exp(-LN60 / (t60 * srate));

    wb[i] = wb0[i] * (1.08 - 0.28 * m);
    we[i] = we0[i] * (0.55 + 0.85 * m);
    i += 1;
  );

  f1 = sf[0];
  f6 = sf[5];
  fmid = sqrt(f1 * f6);
  i = 0;
  loop(6,
    freqNow = sf[i] * exp(lratio[i] * m);
    ff = (log(freqNow) - log(fmid)) / (log(f6) - log(f1));
    dbNow = owdB[i] + MATERIAL_EMISSION_SPAN * 0.5 * ff;
    owc[i] = ow[i] * exp(dbNow * DB_TO_LIN);
    i += 1;
  );

  bodyA = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * (BODY_HZ0 + BODY_HZ1 * m) / srate);

  couplingHz = COUPLING_HZ0 + COUPLING_HZ1 * mh;
  i = 0;
  loop(5,
    cap = 2 * $pi * couplingHz * cmul[i] / srate;
    cap > KAPPA_LIMIT ? cap = KAPPA_LIMIT;
    cap < -KAPPA_LIMIT ? cap = -KAPPA_LIMIT;
    kc[i] = cos(cap);
    ks[i] = sin(cap);
    i += 1;
  );
);

// ============================================================
// BODY / EDGE EXCITATION DECOMPOSITION (per channel, one-pole)
// ============================================================

bodyL += bodyA * (inL - bodyL);
bodyR += bodyA * (inR - bodyR);
edgeL = inL - bodyL;
edgeR = inR - bodyR;

// ============================================================
// SIX MODAL CELLS (per channel, damped two-state rotation)
// Formerly step_bank(); inlined per channel.
// ============================================================

i = 0;
loop(6,
  op = pL[i];
  oq = qL[i];

  drive = exciteSm * (wb[i] * bodyL + we[i] * edgeL) * (1 - rr[i]);

  np = rr[i] * (rc[i] * op - rs[i] * oq) + drive;
  nq = rr[i] * (rs[i] * op + rc[i] * oq);

  pL[i] = np;
  qL[i] = nq;
  i += 1;
);

i = 0;
loop(6,
  op = pR[i];
  oq = qR[i];

  drive = exciteSm * (wb[i] * bodyR + we[i] * edgeR) * (1 - rr[i]);

  np = rr[i] * (rc[i] * op - rs[i] * oq) + drive;
  nq = rr[i] * (rs[i] * op + rc[i] * oq);

  pR[i] = np;
  qR[i] = nq;
  i += 1;
);

// ============================================================
// ENERGY-PRESERVING MODAL COUPLING (alternating Givens lattice)
// Frame A: M1<->M2, M3<->M4, M5<->M6
// Frame B: M2<->M3, M4<->M5
// Redistributes state; never manufactures energy.
// Formerly couple_pair(); inlined.
// ============================================================

coupleToggle < 0.5 ? (
  // pair 0: M1<->M2
  pa = pL[0]; pb = pL[1];
  pL[0] = kc[0] * pa - ks[0] * pb;
  pL[1] = ks[0] * pa + kc[0] * pb;
  qa = qL[0]; qb = qL[1];
  qL[0] = kc[0] * qa - ks[0] * qb;
  qL[1] = ks[0] * qa + kc[0] * qb;
  // pair 1: M3<->M4
  pa = pL[2]; pb = pL[3];
  pL[2] = kc[1] * pa - ks[1] * pb;
  pL[3] = ks[1] * pa + kc[1] * pb;
  qa = qL[2]; qb = qL[3];
  qL[2] = kc[1] * qa - ks[1] * qb;
  qL[3] = ks[1] * qa + kc[1] * qb;
  // pair 2: M5<->M6
  pa = pL[4]; pb = pL[5];
  pL[4] = kc[2] * pa - ks[2] * pb;
  pL[5] = ks[2] * pa + kc[2] * pb;
  qa = qL[4]; qb = qL[5];
  qL[4] = kc[2] * qa - ks[2] * qb;
  qL[5] = ks[2] * qa + kc[2] * qb;
  // right channel, same three pairs
  pa = pR[0]; pb = pR[1];
  pR[0] = kc[0] * pa - ks[0] * pb;
  pR[1] = ks[0] * pa + kc[0] * pb;
  qa = qR[0]; qb = qR[1];
  qR[0] = kc[0] * qa - ks[0] * qb;
  qR[1] = ks[0] * qa + kc[0] * qb;
  pa = pR[2]; pb = pR[3];
  pR[2] = kc[1] * pa - ks[1] * pb;
  pR[3] = ks[1] * pa + kc[1] * pb;
  qa = qR[2]; qb = qR[3];
  qR[2] = kc[1] * qa - ks[1] * qb;
  qR[3] = ks[1] * qa + kc[1] * qb;
  pa = pR[4]; pb = pR[5];
  pR[4] = kc[2] * pa - ks[2] * pb;
  pR[5] = ks[2] * pa + kc[2] * pb;
  qa = qR[4]; qb = qR[5];
  qR[4] = kc[2] * qa - ks[2] * qb;
  qR[5] = ks[2] * qa + kc[2] * qb;
) : (
  // pair 3: M2<->M3
  pa = pL[1]; pb = pL[2];
  pL[1] = kc[3] * pa - ks[3] * pb;
  pL[2] = ks[3] * pa + kc[3] * pb;
  qa = qL[1]; qb = qL[2];
  qL[1] = kc[3] * qa - ks[3] * qb;
  qL[2] = ks[3] * qa + kc[3] * qb;
  // pair 4: M4<->M5
  pa = pL[3]; pb = pL[4];
  pL[3] = kc[4] * pa - ks[4] * pb;
  pL[4] = ks[4] * pa + kc[4] * pb;
  qa = qL[3]; qb = qL[4];
  qL[3] = kc[4] * qa - ks[4] * qb;
  qL[4] = ks[4] * qa + kc[4] * qb;
  // right channel, same two pairs
  pa = pR[1]; pb = pR[2];
  pR[1] = kc[3] * pa - ks[3] * pb;
  pR[2] = ks[3] * pa + kc[3] * pb;
  qa = qR[1]; qb = qR[2];
  qR[1] = kc[3] * qa - ks[3] * qb;
  qR[2] = ks[3] * qa + kc[3] * qb;
  pa = pR[3]; pb = pR[4];
  pR[3] = kc[4] * pa - ks[4] * pb;
  pR[4] = ks[4] * pa + kc[4] * pb;
  qa = qR[3]; qb = qR[4];
  qR[3] = kc[4] * qa - ks[4] * qb;
  qR[4] = ks[4] * qa + kc[4] * qb;
);

coupleToggle = 1 - coupleToggle;

// ============================================================
// MODAL EMISSION + OUTPUT STRUCTURE
// wet = input + materialGain*modal ; out = lerp(input,wet,mix)
// Formerly sum_bank(); inlined.
// ============================================================

modalL = 0;
i = 0;
loop(6,
  modalL += owc[i] * pL[i];
  i += 1;
);
modalR = 0;
i = 0;
loop(6,
  modalR += owc[i] * pR[i];
  i += 1;
);

wetL = inL + MATERIAL_GAIN * modalL;
wetR = inR + MATERIAL_GAIN * modalR;
outL = inL + (wetL - inL) * mixSm;
outR = inR + (wetR - inR) * mixSm;

outL *= outSm;
outR *= outSm;

// emergency containment: fail-safe only; audit proves it never
// activates under nominal probe levels
outL > 0.999 ? ( outL = 0.999; clampCount += 1; );
outL < -0.999 ? ( outL = -0.999; clampCount += 1; );
outR > 0.999 ? ( outR = 0.999; clampCount += 1; );
outR < -0.999 ? ( outR = -0.999; clampCount += 1; );

spl0 = outL + DEAD_DITHER * denormalSign;
spl1 = outR + DEAD_DITHER * denormalSign;

// ============================================================
// STATE HYGIENE (every 1024 samples)
// Denormal scrub + corruption bound: silently snap errant
// state to zero. Normal operation never approaches 8.0; this
// is an emergency barrier, not gain structure.
// ============================================================

scrubCount += 1;
scrubCount >= 1024 ? (
  scrubCount = 0;
  i = 0;
  loop(6,
    abs(pL[i]) < DENORMAL_GUARD ? pL[i] = 0;
    abs(qL[i]) < DENORMAL_GUARD ? qL[i] = 0;
    abs(pR[i]) < DENORMAL_GUARD ? pR[i] = 0;
    abs(qR[i]) < DENORMAL_GUARD ? qR[i] = 0;
    abs(pL[i]) > STATE_BOUND ? pL[i] = 0;
    abs(qL[i]) > STATE_BOUND ? qL[i] = 0;
    abs(pR[i]) > STATE_BOUND ? pR[i] = 0;
    abs(qR[i]) > STATE_BOUND ? qR[i] = 0;
    i += 1;
  );
);
